From de833f820e37e767d3aa3fbf85f33b482668f3f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:21:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Block signals first and stop leaking keymap fds

A SIGUSR1/SIGUSR2/SIGRTMIN that arrived while main() was still doing its
Wayland round trips hit the default action and killed the process; on the
iPAQ the supervisor sends one right after exec. The mask is now built and
applied at the top of main(); the signalfd and handlers are unchanged.

The keymap string was already freed, but create_and_upload_keymap() left
the anonymous file descriptor open and the mmap in place on every upload.
libwayland dups the fd when it marshals the request, so both can be
released right away. With the compose key that is a leak per key press.

tests/check-signals.py connects the binary to a silent fake socket, sends
all handled signals and checks the exit is the binary's own error status.
Upstream-Status: Pending
